  body: "# Evidence after a claim is properly made\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe claims guidance distinguishes
    meeting the prescribed manner of claiming from having sufficient information and evidence for an outcome decision,
    and requires an opportunity to provide requested material.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 02166 contains
    a memo reference and legacy assessed-income-period wording. No current AIP requirement or universal deadline
    is adopted. Benefit-specific response rules and missing-document alternatives remain dependencies.\n\n## Inspected
    source passages\n\n- [DMG 02166, PDF page 48](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68d934f23ff62c51c1a7a2/dmg-v-1-ch-2.pdf#page=48)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 2: Claims.\n- [DMG 02168, PDF page 48](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68d934f23ff62c51c1a7a2/dmg-v-1-ch-2.pdf#page=48)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 2: Claims.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of the 15 September
    2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance, not a consolidated
    statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an
    entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file positions. Machine
    extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve extracted text;
    no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability remain
    separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch2` PDF SHA-256: `218f6a34945a5dd17cdccb1737ea317b2dcfd1ab62f66a9a0b8d681202e8934f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `77cb8966f05e501c4d970026bdfcd5bc271abe17a546b02ec8c8704395e56ee3`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-prescribed-claim
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: A properly made claim can still require evidence or corroboration; these are distinct
      conditions in the passage.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch2/0048
      quote: "02166 [See DMG memo 03/25] A form or document may meet all the criteria to be a claim made in the\n\
        prescribed manner but the information and evidence it contains may be insufficient or need\ncorroboration
        before an outcome decision can be made. The claimant is required to produce any\ncertificates, documents,
        information and evidence as required by the Secretary of State but must be\n\ngiven the opportunity to do
        so1 (for CA this information may be provided electronically - see DMG\n02069). The claimant has a set time
        to reply as specified for each benefit. SPC claimants are required to\nprovide information or evidence as
        to the likelihood of future changes of circumstances so that a\n\ndecision can be made2 on whether an AIP
        should be set and if so of what length. Except where DMG"
      locator: DMG 02166
  - target: term/dmg-outcome-decision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source says that an outcome decision has to be made in the described
      failure-to-provide-evidence cases; it does not prescribe the outcome here.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch2/0048
      quote: "02168 Where\n\n\n1. for benefits other than IS or JSA, a claimant claims in the prescribed manner
        but fails to provide\nadditional information or evidence required under DMG 02166 or\n\n\n2. for IS and
        JSA, a claimant claims in the prescribed manner as described in DMG 02086 but has not\nprovided additional
        information or evidence required under DMG 02166\n\n\nan outcome decision has to be made."
      locator: DMG 02168
